WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.258
Unit twenty. Burns and Scalds!

2
00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:07.729
Hello, everyone! I'm Nurse Bopha, your school nurse.

3
00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:10.855
Hi, Nurse Bopha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.905 --> 00:00:14.708
Today we learn about Burns and Scalds. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.265 --> 00:00:19.398
Burn. Say it with me. Burn!

6
00:00:22.899 --> 00:00:26.166
Scald. Say it with me. Scald!

7
00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:33.450
Cool water. Say it with me. Cool water!

8
00:00:36.949 --> 00:00:40.899
20 minutes. Say it with me. 20 minutes!

9
00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:47.899
Cover. Say it with me. Cover!

10
00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:54.633
Ice. Say it with me. Ice!

11
00:00:58.114 --> 00:01:01.514
Blister. Say it with me. Blister!

12
00:01:05.016 --> 00:01:08.332
Doctor. Say it with me. Doctor!

13
00:01:11.864 --> 00:01:22.592
A scald is a burn from hot liquid or steam. Cool the burn under cool running water for 20 minutes, then cover it loosely. Do not use ice or break a blister, and see a doctor for serious burns.

14
00:01:22.642 --> 00:01:23.792
I can do that too!

15
00:01:25.039 --> 00:01:30.568
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:30.618 --> 00:01:31.835
Cool water!

17
00:01:32.781 --> 00:01:38.027
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:39.227
Blister!

19
00:01:40.184 --> 00:01:46.688
Did you know? Cooling a burn with running water for 20 minutes helps limit the damage to skin!

20
00:01:46.738 --> 00:01:48.842
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:49.711 --> 00:01:57.266
Think and answer. Why should you not put ice on a burn?

22
00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:58.466
Great answer!

23
00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:04.459
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:07.040
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

